{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>gohi</b> — either a verb or an adjective, like gozei (\"cutters off\") from the root גזר, and <b>tigah</b> in \"your rivers\" [Ezekiel 32:2], like motzi'i. He mentioned this because the one who trusts in HaShem, He will deliver him, for behold He is <b>gohi</b> from the womb, when we have neither knowledge nor power."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The verse word גוחי is obscure; Ibn Ezra analyzes it as a form analogous to participial constructs like גוזי and מוציאי, and the second clause ותגח is cited from Ezekiel 32:2 where it likewise lacks a clear derivation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:12.664253419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}